---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactButton from '../components/ContactButton.astro';
const checks = [
 ['check-01','01','Alert gone?','Re-run the scanner on the patch.'],
 ['check-02','02','Attack stopped?','Try the SQL injection cases.'],
 ['check-03','03','Still works?','Compare valid inputs with a correct reference.'],
 ['check-04','04','No shortcuts?','Check that warnings were not suppressed.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Methodology" description="One patch. Four independent checks. A verdict backed by the cases that ran." path="/methodology">
 <article class="method-page shell">
  <header><p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p><h1>The alert is gone.<br/><span>Does it still work?</span></h1><p class="intro">We test the patch against attacks <em>and</em> ordinary use. Closing the warning is only the first check.</p></header>
  <section class="flow" id="contract" aria-label="Patch verification process">
   <div class="flow-end"><span class="eyebrow">Input</span><h2>Your AI’s patch</h2><div class="diff" aria-hidden="true"><span>− unsafe query</span><span>+ proposed fix</span></div><p>Same code. A second opinion.</p></div>
   <div class="checks">{checks.map(([id,n,title,body],i)=><div class="gate" id={id} style={`--step:${i}`}><span class="gate-number">{n}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></div><span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>)}</div>
   <div class="flow-end outcome" id="artifact"><span class="eyebrow">Output</span><h2>A verdict.<br/>With receipts.</h2><p>See which checks passed, what failed, and the inputs behind the result.</p><a href="/benchmark/leaderboard" class="text-link">See pilot results ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <p class="flow-caption">Illustration of the method · hosted patch scoring is not live yet</p>
  <section class="verdict-section"><h2>Three possible outcomes.</h2><div class="verdict-grid"><div><span class="status-dot pass"></span><h3>Verified</h3><p>All four checks passed for the tested cases.</p></div><div><span class="status-dot fail"></span><h3>Not verified</h3><p>At least one check failed. The evidence shows where.</p></div><div><span class="status-dot"></span><h3>Insufficient evidence</h3><p>The run could not establish a result. Never a pass.</p></div></div><p class="scope-note">A pass is evidence for these cases, not a guarantee that the whole application is secure.</p></section>
  <section class="scope" id="limitations"><div><p class="eyebrow">Where we are today</p><h2>SQL injection.<br/>Four test cases.</h2></div><div><p>Our current benchmark uses seeded Python/SQLite modules: quoted strings, numbers, ORDER BY and second-order injection.</p><p>Small samples and published tests have limits. The blind pilot kept test cases from the fixer; the public benchmark is a separate exercise.</p><a href="/benchmark/01/#submit" class="text-link">Open the patch form ↗</a></div></section>
  <details class="reference-links" id="terms"><summary>Scope, evidence and technical details</summary><div id="index-rules"><p>Early demonstrations tested three constructed patches. Provider results come from the separate blind pilot. The proposed real-project Index is not live. No-alert records are reported separately from scored patches.</p></div><p id="harness"><span id="harness-scope">The backend is designed to run patches in isolated Docker containers with resource limits and a timeout. It needs a separate deployed service; Vercel hosts this website.</span></p><p id="assumptions">Results depend on test coverage, an executable environment and a trustworthy reference. They do not establish safety for other languages or vulnerability classes.</p><p id="method-version"><a href="/research/methodology-v1">Detailed method reference</a> · <a href="/evidence">Reports and source artifacts</a></p><p id="disputes">A fix can close the hole and quietly break a real user. Inspect the evidence and its limitations before relying on a verdict.</p></details>
  <div class="reading-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/benchmark">Explore the benchmark ↗</a><ContactButton /></div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.method-page h1,.method-page h2,.method-page h3{font-family:Inter,sans-serif}.method-page{padding-top:54px;padding-bottom:80px}.method-page header{max-width:760px;margin-bottom:48px}.method-page h1{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,76px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:20px 0 24px}.method-page h1 span{color:var(--acc)}.intro{font-size:19px;color:var(--fg-2);max-width:580px;line-height:1.6}.intro em{font-style:normal;color:var(--fg)}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr 1fr;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--panel)}.flow-end{padding:32px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}.flow h2{font-size:26px;letter-spacing:-.035em;line-height:1.15;margin:16px 0}.flow p{font-size:14px;color:var(--fg-2);line-height:1.6}.diff{font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;display:grid;gap:9px;padding:20px 0}.diff span:first-child{color:var(--fail)}.diff span:last-child{color:var(--acc)}.checks{border-inline:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px;background:var(--bg-2)}.gate{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:20px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.gate:last-child{border-bottom:0}.gate h3{font-size:17px;margin:0 0 4px}.gate p{margin:0;font-size:12px}.gate-number{font:12px monospace;color:var(--acc)}.pulse{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--acc);margin-left:auto;flex-shrink:0;animation:gate-scan 4s ease calc(var(--step)*.65s) 1 both}.outcome .text-link{margin-top:20px}.flow-caption{font:11px monospace;color:var(--fg-3);margin-top:14px}.verdict-section{padding:64px 0 42px}.method-page h2{letter-spacing:-.035em}.verdict-section>h2,.scope h2{font-size:32px;line-height:1.15}.verdict-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:32px;margin-top:30px}.verdict-grid h3{font-size:17px;margin:14px 0 8px}.verdict-grid p,.scope p,.reference-links p{color:var(--fg-2);font-size:14px;line-height:1.65}.status-dot{display:block;width:20px;height:4px;background:#9c97a4}.status-dot.pass{background:#aad4b8}.status-dot.fail{background:#e99e9e}.scope-note{color:var(--fg-3);font-size:12px;margin-top:25px}.scope{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.7fr;gap:50px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:38px 0}.scope p{margin-bottom:14px}.reference-links{border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px 0}.reference-links summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:14px}.reference-links p{margin-top:16px}.reference-links a{color:var(--acc)}:global(:root[data-theme="light"]) .status-dot{background:var(--fg-3)}:global(:root[data-theme="light"]) .status-dot.pass{background:var(--acc)}:global(:root[data-theme="light"]) .status-dot.fail{background:var(--fail)}@keyframes gate-scan{0%,100%{opacity:.45;box-shadow:0 0 0 0 transparent}40%,70%{opacity:1;box-shadow:0 0 0 6px #c4afff18}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.pulse{animation:none}}@media(max-width:760px){.method-page{padding-top:40px}.flow{grid-template-columns:1fr}.checks{border-inline:0;border-block:1px solid var(--line)}.flow-end{padding:24px}.verdict-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.verdict-grid>div{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:20px}.scope{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px}.flow-caption{line-height:1.6}}
</style>
